NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: The headline ("prefix-family-aware batch admission") is RENAMING of an already-published
mechanism (SGLang cache-aware scheduling). The only candidate MECHANISM delta is the bounded reorder window
(W) with an explicit p99 fairness cap — and that is a thin composition of two known ideas: cache-aware
admission (SGLang/vLLM/Preble) + classic aging/starvation-bound scheduling, of which VTC is the LLM-serving
instance. Not a new mechanism; a fairness-controlled RE-MEASUREMENT of a known one.

FATAL_COLLISIONS:
- SGLang cache-aware scheduling == the claim's core admission mechanism (kills "achieves higher hit rate
  than FCFS by co-scheduling a prefix family" as novel).
- The "unbounded-W greedy" variant the researcher reports (+17% @ 1.29-1.34x p99) is essentially SGLang's
  default greedy cache-aware sort — i.e. the paper's own baseline is prior art, not a new policy.

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK: SGLang/RadixAttention (2312.07104); vLLM APC; Preble (2407.00023); VTC/Fairness in
Serving (2401.00588). Strongly recommended: chunked-prefill scheduling (Sarathi-Serve, OSDI'24, 2403.02310)
since the GPU-pass ask explicitly touches it.

RATIONALE: The claim as written collides head-on with SGLang cache-aware scheduling (NeurIPS'24) and is
independently anticipated by vLLM APC and Preble — ≥2 independent published sources for the core mechanism.
The researcher already concedes this and narrows the contribution to the matched-fairness control; but that
residual is incremental (cache-aware admission + bounded aging) and overlaps VTC's fairness-bounded
scheduling. RED on novelty-as-claimed: the L0 is a competent, honest re-measurement with a fairness control,
NOT a new mechanism, and it cannot proceed to a novelty claim without (a) reframing the contribution to ONLY
the fairness-bounded comparison and (b) a head-to-head against SGLang's actual cache-aware scheduler (not a
hand-rolled FCFS baseline) showing the bounded-W p99 cap buys something VTC+SGLang does not.
